WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.309
The method takes the number of trees to infinity.

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:06.145
For perfect binary soft trees of depth d,

00:00:06.225 --> 00:00:12.301
the authors prove the Tree Neural Tangent Kernel
converges to a deterministic kernel with

00:00:12.381 --> 00:00:17.143
two parts: one from the inner splitting nodes and
one from the leaves.

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:20.187
The soft split uses a scaled error function,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.576
a smooth sigmoid whose sharpness is set by alpha,

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:28.141
and its expectations have closed forms, so the
kernel is analytic.

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:32.015
Because the kernel stays constant and positive definite,

00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:36.303
training reduces to kernel regression with global
convergence,

00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:41.560
and the formula is not recursive in depth, so its
cost is depth-independent.
